{{also|round up|Roundup}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From the verb phrase {{m|en|round up}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|US|agriculture}} An activity in which [[cattle]] are [[herded]] together in order to be [[inspected]], [[counted]], [[branded]] or [[shipped]].
# {{lb|en|law enforcement}} The similar [[police]] activity of [[gathering]] together [[suspect]]s to a [[crime]].
# The [[summary]] to a [[news]] [[bulletin]].
# An [[upward]] [[curvature]] or [[convexity]], as in the [[deck]] of a [[vessel]]. <!--in W1913 given as "round-up"-->

